{"skill":{"slug":"self-improving-agent-cn","displayName":"Self Improving Agent CN"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1772795365586,"changelog":"Initial release of AI自我改进与记忆系统:\n\n- 自动捕获、记录命令错误、用户纠正与最佳实践并转为长期记忆\n- 支持跨项目同步与全局+项目级记忆管理\n- 执行前智能检查相关记忆，规避重复犯错\n- 触发机制自动化，无需手动干预\n- 重要经验自动更新至 AGENTS.md、MEMORY.md 等文档\n- 增强与原有 self-improvement skill 的对比与兼容","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4270,"sha256":"2f779a9025ae04fca38c6490afa235846c8c79ec77d8dbd2d471806ba34520be","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"check_memory.py","size":2653,"sha256":"343d58a3a2b6e5d8feaddf2737fa385ab4c13edcf5d8698f60554b66d0ba6368","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"log_best_practice.py","size":1401,"sha256":"3abd982d920af05296944c949681b05a0c2257c833fdaaf41b55abbf4dd0d326","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"log_correction.py","size":1951,"sha256":"b0fb32468cebf45bc153b86271c3f1d8ab11cd665e485f22c4f0c163b5ccf04a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"log_error.py","size":1431,"sha256":"cc06500b5b9e0334facdf87b3266735a7dcf097dc09fc59bd6aad79d4aa65759","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill.json","size":345,"sha256":"5eee23f959e4fd83c65d30e99033c1a0c3dfe39fecc84f4ddff40674e697a3aa","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2178,"sha256":"622851aac251c59f30880ed853cd1aac20a2448657a6930597e77d6d200ee22b","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789108742523,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"79441ecd80a95447da03b82e9ac9b1bb8d0e0208794f52995c72c2d8e335de44","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/79441ecd80a95447da03b82e9ac9b1bb8d0e0208794f52995c72c2d8e335de44","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780089780835},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789108742523},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed self-improvement memory system, but it automatically stores and reuses user corrections and command failures in ways that can persistently change future agent behavior without enough user control.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill writes global memory and instructs synchronization to current-project .learnings, AGENTS.md, and MEMORY.md. That is high-impact for an agent-behavior skill because project files may be version-controlled or reused across sessions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is simple local file usage with no remote payloads or package dependencies observed. It creates a predictable global memory directory under ~/.openclaw/memory/self-improving but does not define restrictive permissions or a permissions boundary.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Automatic triggers such as broad correction phrases and command failures are under-scoped, and the retrieved records are presented as recommendations or corrections without labeling them as untrusted data or requiring confirmation before reuse.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent plaintext storage is central to the skill, but it has no enforced redaction, retention, approval, or deletion controls. It also includes examples where a future command may automatically switch to sudo after a prior permission failure.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the scripts: logging errors, corrections, and best practices, then checking them later. The concern is that the skill also tells the agent to automatically promote memories into AGENTS.md and MEMORY.md, turning free-form user or tool text into persistent agent guidance.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. It is not showing remote execution or hidden exfiltration, but it can persist user text, command failures, and suggested fixes into long-term memory and agent instruction files. Only use it if you are comfortable with automatic memory writes, and avoid letting it save secrets, raw command lines, or sudo-based fixes without explicit review.","findings":"[T02] unexpected: Artifact evidence supports the core concern: log_correction.py and log_error.py persist free-form corrections and fixes, check_memory.py resurfaces them, and SKILL.md instructs promotion into AGENTS.md and MEMORY.md. This is not malicious by itself, but it is an under-controlled persistent instruction channel.\n[T09] unexpected: The scripts store commands, errors, corrections, and practices verbatim in plaintext JSONL files under a predictable memory directory. The documentation says sensitive information should be desensitized, but the code does not enforce redaction or restrictive file permissions.\n[LP3] unexpected: The file operations are purpose-related, but the artifact lacks a clear permission boundary and includes writes beyond the dedicated memory directory, including project .learnings, AGENTS.md, and MEMORY.md.\n[RA2] unexpected: Cross-session memory is the disclosed purpose, but the retention is indefinite and can affect later sessions and projects without approval, review, or expiration controls.\n[AS3] expected: The cited command reads this skill's own SKILL.md after installation; I did not find artifact evidence of enumerating or reading other installed skills.\n[PE2] unexpected: The sudo examples are not hidden, but they are unsafe as automatic remediation guidance because they can normalize elevated package installation across later tasks.\n[SSD-3] unexpected: Persisting user corrections is purpose-aligned, but the artifact stores plain-language user data durably and proposes copying it into instruction-bearing project files without clear consent or minimization.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The automatic capture triggers are broad natural-language fragments, making accidental or context-poor persistence plausible.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The documentation explicitly says important memories automatically sync to global storage, project .learnings, AGENTS.md, and MEMORY.md, which is too broad without opt-in controls.\n[SQP-3] expected: The skill is Chinese-language and the identifier includes a cn suffix, so I treat the language issue as a locale/audience note rather than a security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789108742523}}}}}